# QuorumForge deliberation — line-oriented (.qf) format
# ------------------------------------------------------
# Topic: is the distributed cache coherent under concurrent writes?
# This file exercises consensus, contested, split, and unsupported outcomes.
#
# Grammar reminder (see docs/EVIDENCE.md):
#   delib | <id> | <question>
#   agent | <id> | <name> | <weight> | <role>
#   claim | <id> | <topic> | <text>
#   pos   | <agent> | <claim> | <stance> | <confidence> | <note>
#   cite  | <agent> | <claim> | <source> | <locator>

delib | cache-coherence | Is the distributed write-back cache coherent under concurrent writes?

# --- Council ---------------------------------------------------------------
agent | ada    | Ada Reyes      | 1.6 | systems-verification
agent | boro   | Boro Kanel     | 1.0 | performance-skeptic
agent | cyan   | Cyan Okafor    | 1.3 | formal-methods
agent | dice   | Dice Vardhan   | 0.8 | field-operations
agent | echo   | Echo Lindqvist | 1.1 | correctness-review

# --- Claims ----------------------------------------------------------------
claim | c1 | linearizability | Writes to a single key are linearizable.
claim | c2 | linearizability | Writes across multiple keys are linearizable.
claim | c3 | recovery        | The cache recovers a consistent state after a node crash.
claim | c4 | performance     | Coherence traffic stays below 5% of total bandwidth.
